<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 4 Best in Slot Gear list for Protection Paladin Tank in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Icecrown Citadel. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, BoE World drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 4</h2>Phase 4 is the conclusive end of the expansion, and what better ending could be hoped for than to climb the steps of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> and to do battle with <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_lichking.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a> himself at the top. Naturally to do so we need to prepare and set up our characters for the coming challenges. First off, for any new or returning <a class="icontiny c2" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/paladin">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_paladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Paladin</span></a>
<span class="c2">s</span> phase 4 will give us 3 new dungeons in; <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4809/the-forge-of-souls">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Forge of Souls</span></a>, <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4813/pit-of-saron">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Pit of Saron</span></a>, and <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4820/halls-of-reflection">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Halls of Reflection</span></a> to explore. In total you now have a very broad avenue to gear up through RDF and dungeon content.<br/>
<br/>For many of you though, this is no longer about gearing up to face the Lich King, you are already primed and ready to start your progression. For you, there are some new and some familiar challenges in this phase, for those that <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4273/ulduar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ulduar</span></a> raided may remember <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_algalon_01.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=32871/algalon-the-observer">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Algalon the Observer</span></a>, while the Lich King have more differences than similarities with Algalon they both represent bosses with a high potential of killing the tank due to overwhelming damage. To combat this, to those coming from the relatively lax and safe encounters of phase 3 (save one VERY angry yeti) we strongly recommend that you take a moment and revisit your gems in preparation for ICC, this content phase seriously favors a large health bar and strong cooldowns.<br/>
<br/>For those that played <span style="color: green;">
<img alt="" class="no-border" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/icons/bc.gif"/> TBC</span> may remember <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=45769/sunwell-radiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_circleofrenewal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sunwell Radiance</span></a>, in an addition absolutely no one asked for we get version 2.0 in the form of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69127/chill-of-the-throne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_zone_icecrown_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Chill of the Throne</span></a>. Never fear though, this one is worse as it applies after diminishing returns, meaning that your stats are still being heavily taxed (diminished). This debuff applies to the enemies encountered inside <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> and works akin to enemy expertise, letting them bypass a huge portion of your dodge. Buffs like <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70761/item-paladin-t10-protection-4p-bonus">our 4-piece tier 10</a> is not affected by this.<ul>
<li class="fa fa-comment">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<i>Gearing for progression in phase 4 &amp; the role of resistances in ICC</i></b>
<br/>ICC is a major step up in difficulty, not only in required raid coordination and orientation but also contain a few stand out fights that will put your survivability on trial. It's worth noting as per usual, no amount of gear will offset your inability to pilot your character, whether it is a poorly performed rotation or bad/<wbr/>lacking CD usage. The latter is key to surviving many of the most dangerous fights of this expansion before you. This is all to say that your survivability is paramount in phase 4, it will be in your interest to potentially adjust your existing gem and enchant set-up and prioritize stamina for your progression.<br/>
<br/>This phase also contain fights which you can gear specifically towards <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_sindragosa.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a>, prime consort of Malygos himself is the 11th boss in ICC. Her fight mirrors <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=15989/sapphiron">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sapphiron</span></a> from <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=3456/naxxramas">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Naxxramas</span></a>, in a lot of ways; both have the typical dragon frontal cleave, tail swipe, frost damage aura, and a <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">powerful frost breath</a>, as well as a <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70128/mystic-buffet">ramping magic damage aura</a>. It's these latter two that we are the most concerned with, her melee damage is one of the highest in the game and can be paired with her breath to form a very effective way to quickly kill the tank. She is also capable of parry-hasting, meaning Sindragosa is capable of rapidly and randomly bursting your tank at any given point in the fight.<br/>
<br/>To properly engage with her on progression, we then suggest that you; make sure you are expertise capped at +56 expertise skill in order to suppress her ability to parry you, carry some amount of frost resistance in order to reduce the weight of the heavy combo potential she has. Items that are stand out for these purposes are; <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49475/judgement-heaume">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_74.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Judgement Heaume</span></a>, which through its dense stamina and hit budgetting it permits you to carry additional expertise or resistance in other slots, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49489/signified-ring-of-binding">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Signified Ring of Binding</span></a> which is perfectly itemized for this fight, and ofcourse the dedicated frost resistance kit <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=43582/titanium-frostguard-ring">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_57.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Titanium Frostguard Ring</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=43587/icebane-girdle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_33.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Icebane Girdle</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>There is also the resistance enchant kit in the form of <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=44137/arcanum-of-the-frosty-soul">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frozencore.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Frosty Soul</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=44483/enchant-cloak-superior-frost-resistance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulagood_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Cloak - Superior Frost Resistance</span></a>, leatherworkers may also apply <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=57694/fur-lining-frost-resist">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_leatherworking.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Frost Resist</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-shield">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>
<i>Utilizing CDs and things to look out for</i></b>
<br/>
<br/>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_lichking.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36597/the-lich-king">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Lich King</span></a> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>, this single-target nuke <b>hits for a whopping 70k on heroic!</b> It can be partially resisted but needs to be handled by a cooldown in almost every circumstance, generally you taunt swap as this lands, the new tank is also liable to die without cooldown usage as the secondary effect of <b>increases the caster's haste by 100% for 5 sec.</b> will make the boss hit seriously fast. <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37698/shambling-horror">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shambling Horror</span></a> will cast <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=72143/enrage">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enrage</span></a>, you will need to cc (stun) or use a CD to absorb this.<br/>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_sindragosa.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36853/sindragosa">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa</span></a> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a> does major frost damage, while it's not harmless however generally not lethal even at relatively low frost resistance levels in phase 1. She has a severe ramp up mechanic in the last phase through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=70128/mystic-buffet">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_arcane_arcane03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mystic Buffet</span></a>, which means that at the very least every instance of frost breath should be precipitated by a cooldown.<br/>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_festergutrotface.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>'s high damage ramps up even harder the longer the fight goes on, the boss will stack <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69165/inhale-blight">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_festergutrotface.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inhale Blight</span></a> as the fight progresses and we suggest that you manage this with continously rolling cooldowns when at 2 and 3 stacks.<br/>
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/achievement_boss_saurfang.gif");'></span>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37813/deathbringer-saurfang">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathbringer Saurfang</span></a> this boss energy bar represents a corresponding increase in damage through <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=72371/blood-power">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_deathknight_bloodpresence.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blood Power</span></a> what this means is that at 99 blood power, he does 99% more damage. This naturally hurts but the entire fight is about handling his energy bar and it becomes devastating once he reaches 30% health and activates <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=72737/frenzy">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_deathpact.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frenzy</span></a>. You should be rolling cooldowns, not only at +60-70 blood power, but also continuously after 30%.</div></li></ul>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="gems">Gems</h4>When planning your gems, you will want to use your slots to balance out your hit, defense and match your meta gem requirement. It's generally not advised to match socket bonuses carelessly,  Most often it is not worthwhile to get the gem bonus unless it's a minimum +6 stamina per gem bonus. For a longer discussion and info on gems, see the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/guide/classes/paladin/protection/tank-enchants-gems-pve">Gem Guide.</a>
