<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="ruby-sanctum">Updates for Best in Slot Gear in Ruby Sanctum</h3>
<a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4987/the-ruby-sanctum">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Ruby Sanctum</span></a> is a one-boss raid who drops Lich King equivalent item-level gear. It doesn't have that much to offer us tanks but if you've been starved of feet upgrades from ICC <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54579/treads-of-impending-resurrection">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Treads of Impending Resurrection</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54564/scions-treads">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Scion's Treads</span></a> could be some pretty good upgrades for you. The raid does offer <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54591/petrified-twilight-scale">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubysanctum3.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Petrified Twilight Scale</span></a> to tanks, though it's solidly behind the ICC and badge options. For those that want to utilize the ICC buff and maybe gear a little more aggressively you could compete with your DPS for <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=54578/apocalypses-advance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Apocalypse's Advance</span></a>, while not advised plate dps gear with hit on it could be put to good use in certain sets. That said, we're not lacking for hit in any regard in ICC so we say just skip this one.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="emblems">Emblems of Frost for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 4</h3>Emblems play a larger role in our gearing than ever before, as you now have to actually purchase previous tiers of gear in order to acquire the highest item-level on tier. This is to say tier works like a ladder, you have to start from the lowest item level and pay an initial emblem cost and then further tokens to keep upgrading your gear. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> are primarily acquired from Raiding in phase 4, both 10 and 25-man <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4812/icecrown-citadel">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Icecrown Citadel</span></a> will drop a total of 25 emblems per full clear, in addition of this <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=37126/sister-svalna">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sister Svalna</span></a> also award one emblem. As usual <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/zone=4603/vault-of-archavon">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Vault of Archavon</span></a> will be updated with an additional boss this phase, <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=38433/toravon-the-ice-watcher">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Toravon the Ice Watcher</span></a> which award you 2 additional emblems per kill in both 10 and 25-man. You may also acquire emblems through doing heroic dungeons and weekly raid quests.<br/>
<br/>All tier will require an emblem buy-in, head, chest, and legs all require 95 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> each, while shoulders and gloves 60 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49426/emblem-of-frost">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_frostemblem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Emblem of Frost</span></a> each. Tier this phase all build into your finalized best in slot set, making up some of the strongest and most well rounded gear available to us in this entire phase, meaning tier purchases automatically are a never miss situation as they will always build into some of the best gear available to you. The only stand out tier item that you will probably not rush to purchase are the shoulders as their upgraded form has an already competitive side-grade, and is only better if you do not have any other choice but the shoulder to acquire your set bonuses from.<br/>
<br/>Note that if you want to go the route of upgrading into tier 10 first, to arrange it with your guild or group, so that you do not go in blind expecting tier upgrade tokens if they're being distributed to other players first.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> is an outstanding trinket that is slated to be a mainstay #2 BiS trinket for the remainder of this phase, highly recommended item. The question is whether you want to prioritize upgrading this, if you are coming directly from the previous tiers, this does offer a significant upgrade over your <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45158/heart-of-iron">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_spiritshard_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Iron</span></a>, we recommend that this item be your #3 or #5 emblem item that you purchase. The on-use is weaker than what we are used to at this point, but still very strong when effectively applied prior to incoming damage. This item can be delayed in favor of rapidly acquiring and upgrading your tier if you already have the highly lucrative <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> from last phase.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50991/verdigris-chain-belt">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_62.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Verdigris Chain Belt</span></a>, sits as a solid belt option for this phase, though unlike many of the other bonus armor pieces, it's not as generous with its additional mitigation as other slots, meaning that if or when you pick this up, do it after you have settled all other emblem affairs.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50461/libram-of-the-eternal-tower">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Libram of the Eternal Tower</span></a> is the best avoidance relic slot item in the game, however the presence of strong diminishing returns and the low impact of dodge in general means that we'll prioritize past librams over this one.<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50968/cataclysmic-chestguard">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cataclysmic Chestguard</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50978/gauntlets-of-the-kraken">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_86.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gauntlets of the Kraken</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50466/sentinels-winter-cloak">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sentinel's Winter Cloak</span></a> are all solid items in their own right and are competitive across the board in terms of physical damage mitigation they will provide, versus even the strongest pieces in the game. That said, physical damage is not the primary concern for us in this phase, our mitigation is already very solid and we want to primarily look to raising our health pool and for that they are all generally worse than their raid drop counterparts.<br/>
<br/>
