<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="trinkets">Trinkets for Protection Paladin Tank Phase 4</h3>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> great but boring trinket to capstone this expansion, it's amazing for both its raw stamina and its on-use. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50356/corroded-skeleton-key">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_key_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Corroded Skeleton Key</span></a> vs <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> boil down to the window you are comparing them through, the former is very strong and capable against singular attacks in a short timeframe (think first hit <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69409/soul-reaper">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_shadowdance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Reaper</span></a>, or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=69649/frost-breath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_frost_frostnova.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frost Breath</span></a>) but very weak against sustained damage like <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/npc=36626/festergut">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Festergut</span></a>'s rapid and strong melees. In contrast <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47451/juggernauts-vitality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_scarab_crystal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Vitality</span></a> has weaker stats up front, though a much stronger on-use across a larger window of damage. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50344/unidentifiable-organ">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_ore_feliron_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unidentifiable Organ</span></a> may be a little bit of a dark horse in this phase, on paper very solid, with the highest potential EHP out of any trinket in the game when fully stacked, though due to the prevalence of tank swapping or encounters where you are periodically not taking any melee attacks this is unreliable even in the best of cases.<br/>
<br/>DPS trinkets remain good, with the newest addition in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50706/tiny-abomination-in-a-jar">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_enchantedvial.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tiny Abomination in a Jar</span></a> we have more options than ever. This trinket is very solid, however may be hard to equip (as well as obtain) as you are fairly liable to overcap on hit rating with this equipped, in order to get the most out of this trinket you will have to swap a lot of consumables or gear around to make it work.<div class="pad"></div>
